# The ShellCheck release the gate holds its actionlint step to, pinned here and
# nowhere else: the ci workflow reads this file to install the analyzer, and
# the gate reads it again to refuse actionlint unless the installed binary
# reports this release.
#
# actionlint shells out to ShellCheck when it finds one on PATH and says
# nothing at all when it does not, so a host without it reports a pass for an
# analysis nobody ran. Holding every host to the same release is what makes
# the matrix legs read a script the same way.
#
# ShellCheck is neither a crates.io package nor a Go program, so it joins
# neither .github/cargo-tools nor .github/go-tools. This file holds a bare
# release the way .bun-version does, and the ci workflow joins the tool name
# on to build the coordinate its installer takes.
#
# Nothing bumps this automatically. Dependabot has no ecosystem for a release
# binary, so a human edits this file.
0.11.0
